# Vue Code Style

## Component structure
- Always use `<script setup lang="ts">` (Composition API)
- Order: `<script setup>` → `<template>` → `<style>` (if needed)
- One component per file, PascalCase filename (e.g. CampaignList.vue)

## TypeScript
- Use `defineProps<{}>()` and `defineEmits<>()` — no runtime declarations
- Prefer `interface` over `type` for props and data shapes
- Use `ref` for primitives, `reactive` for objects
- Use `computed()` for all derived data (drop-off %, conversion rate)

## Styling
- Tailwind v4 classes only — no inline styles, no scoped CSS unless unavoidable
- Mobile-first responsive design

## Logic
- Extract reusable logic into composables (`src/composables/`)
- Keep template logic minimal — calculations belong in `computed` or composables
- Use `v-memo` only if rendering performance is visibly an issue

## Naming
- Variables: camelCase with auxiliary verbs (`isLoading`, `hasError`, `selectedCampaign`)
- Composables: `use` prefix (`useCampaigns`, `useFunnelMetrics`)
- Directories: lowercase with dashes (`funnel-step`, `campaign-detail`)

## What NOT to use
- No Pinia (not installed, not needed)
- No Options API
- No classes
- No enums — use string literal types instead
